{"id":"heth","name":"Heth","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:heth"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Heth","text":"Dread, a descendant of Canaan, and the ancestor of the Hittites (Gen. 10:18; Deut. 7:1), who dwelt in the vicinity of Hebron (Gen. 23:3, 7). The Hittites were a Hamitic race. They are called “the sons of Heth” (Gen. 23:3, 5, 7, 10, 16, 18, 20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2845","lemma":"חֵת","xlit":"Chêth","gloss":"Cheth, an aboriginal Canaanite","kjv":"Heth","count":10,"share":1},{"strong":"H85","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","xlit":"ʼAbrâhâm","gloss":"Abraham, the later name of Abram","kjv":"Abraham","count":6,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H6085","lemma":"עֶפְרוֹן","xlit":"ʻEphrôwn","gloss":"Ephron, the name of a Canaanite and of two places in Pal","kjv":"Ephron, Ephrain","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H6721","lemma":"צִידוֹן","xlit":"Tsîydôwn","gloss":"Tsidon, the name of a son of Canaan, and of a place in P","kjv":"Sidon, Zidon","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H3667","lemma":"כְּנַעַן","xlit":"Kᵉnaʻan","gloss":"Kenaan, a son a Ham","kjv":"Canaan, merchant, traffick","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H1060","lemma":"בְּכוֹר","xlit":"bᵉkôwr","gloss":"firstborn","kjv":"eldest, firstborn","count":2,"share":0.2}],"verses":["Gen.10.15","Gen.23.3","Gen.23.5","Gen.23.7","Gen.23.10","Gen.23.16","Gen.23.18","Gen.27.46","Gen.49.32","1Chr.1.13"],"related":[{"id":"hittites","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"hittites","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.096,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"cave","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.073,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"land","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.041,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"burial","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.029,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abimelech","type":"lexical","strong":"H85","why":"both lead with אַבְרָהָם (H85)"},{"id":"abraham